1
00:00:01,021 --> 00:00:03,259
Two completed tasks in your index.

2
00:00:03,343 --> 00:00:04,432
Two on the chain.

3
00:00:04,748 --> 00:00:07,393
The totals match, but the tasks do not.

4
00:00:07,709 --> 00:00:10,362
Reorg Lab makes that failure reproducible on

5
00:00:10,367 --> 00:00:11,630
a local EVM.

6
00:00:11,946 --> 00:00:14,045
The command line runs the experiment.

7
00:00:14,129 --> 00:00:15,494
This browser is a viewer for

8
00:00:15,499 --> 00:00:16,704
its saved report.

9
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:20,465
Branch A completes tasks forty-two and ninety-nine.

10
00:00:20,724 --> 00:00:23,157
The runner restores only the node, keeping the

11
00:00:23,162 --> 00:00:25,342
indexer's JSON file intact.

12
00:00:25,658 --> 00:00:27,803
Branch B completes seven and nine.

13
00:00:27,852 --> 00:00:29,417
Both heads are block three.

14
00:00:29,675 --> 00:00:31,019
Their hashes differ.

15
00:00:31,335 --> 00:00:34,662
A deliberately flawed cursor checks only height, fetches

16
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:38,029
nothing, and keeps the wrong history: two orphaned

17
00:00:38,034 --> 00:00:40,655
rows, with two canonical rows missing.

18
00:00:40,971 --> 00:00:43,567
The recovering adapter finds the common ancestor

19
00:00:43,572 --> 00:00:44,614
at block one.

20
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:46,992
It removes the old rows and replays

21
00:00:46,997 --> 00:00:48,375
the canonical events.

22
00:00:48,692 --> 00:00:52,007
The report compares exact event identities and task

23
00:00:52,012 --> 00:00:55,260
state with contract reads and a clean reconstruction.

24
00:00:55,576 --> 00:00:58,207
This run records seven passing checks and two

25
00:00:58,212 --> 00:01:00,415
expected inconclusive outcomes.

26
00:01:00,731 --> 00:01:04,395
Insufficient history and an interrupted RPC read leave

27
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,510
the stored index unchanged.

28
00:01:06,826 --> 00:01:09,180
They do not count as successful recovery.

29
00:01:09,659 --> 00:01:12,383
After a task is reopened, a second projector

30
00:01:12,388 --> 00:01:15,252
also agrees with the contract's completion counter.

31
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:19,316
Seventeen automated tests cover this local implementation.

32
00:01:19,701 --> 00:01:22,775
Reproduce the experiment locally with the command shown.

33
00:01:23,092 --> 00:01:26,094
This is real local bytecode execution, not a

34
00:01:26,099 --> 00:01:29,149
mainnet reorganization or a production guarantee.

35
00:01:29,465 --> 00:01:31,529
The browser cannot run the EVM.

36
00:01:31,579 --> 00:01:33,443
Inspect the evidence behind a total

37
00:01:33,448 --> 00:01:34,432
that looks right.
